---
title: Columns and grids
---

# Columns and grids

`\{% columns %}` places its children in equal-width columns, side by side.
Each column is either a list item (`*`) or a blank-line-separated block. The
`gap` attribute (points) sets the spacing, and `widths` (e.g. `widths="2 1"`
or `widths=[2, 1]`) makes them uneven. `align="center"` centres each column's
content, and `background="#…"` paints a panel behind the row. For a set of
cells that should *reflow* into as many columns as fit — wrapping into rows —
reach for `\{% grid %}` (at the end). Render with `--assets-root examples` so
the swatch images resolve.

## Two images — list form

{% columns %}
* ![](swatch.png)
* ![](swatch.svg)
{% /columns %}

